1	diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
2	index 2e87ffd..b337aa9 100644
3	--- a/README.md
4	+++ b/README.md
5	@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@ The race is for rubbings (§4; the slice plays Sun and Moon, two sealed sources
6	 
7	 Fruit powers join the race (§9). Four fruit pedestals, two Ember and two Smoke, stand at island docks; a pedestal in sight shows whether it still holds its fruit. Moored at a pedestal's dock, press F to read its kit: the two specials and what they're good for. Hold F for three seconds to eat it. Letting go, casting off, a grapple or a disconnect stops the meal, and if two captains finish together the fruit goes to one of them. The kit replaces your two specials (U, I) in every duel at sea for the rest of the match, even after a defeat. A duel shows both fighters' kits. The arena draws Ember's flame bolts and Smoke's smoke screens, and a fighter inside a screen still shows a startup flash, its position and its health.
8	 
9	+Every captain starts with a rumor (§3): an island where a rubbing type they lack is still sealed, or a sector with a recovery cache holding one. Press M for the journal: your rumors with why you got them (start, fresh, targeted, replacement, sighting), stale ones greyed out with what replaced them, the islands you have seen and whether their ruin is open, your types and your kit. A rumor whose target is emptied goes stale and is replaced; losing a rubbing in a duel gives a free fresh lead (§11); when every copy of a type is carried, the lead is a coarse carrier sighting, 30 to 60 seconds old. Moored at any dock, the journal sells a targeted rumor about a type you lack for 25 gold (Tab to its button, Enter), charged only when a lead is delivered. The sea shows its sector borders while the journal is open or a sector rumor is active.
10	+
11	 The standalone duel (the combat spike, §18 stage 1) runs beside it: "Create duel" makes a 1v1 duel whose code the second browser enters under "Join duel", and "Practice" fights a server-side dummy (idle or guarding). After a three-second countdown both browsers predict the fight with the shared duel simulation and roll back to the server's inputs (`docs/duel.md`). Keys (§8): WASD or the arrows move (hold back to guard), J light, K heavy, U and I specials, Shift dash, J and K together throw. The HUD shows both health bars, stamina, the round clock, the connection line (round trip, input delay, corrections) and the result; "Show hitboxes" draws hurtboxes and active hitboxes.
12	 
13	 ## Requirements
